ion] ORB360_CW. A turntable-style 360-degree camera orbit of <Subject 1>, keeping the background and lighting seen in <Picture 1>, <Picture 2> and <Picture 3>.\n\nretention_analysis:\n<Subject 1> (appears in [Shot 1]): fully_preserved - its geometry, proportions, materials, colors, markings and surface details are retained, and it stays completely frozen.\n<Picture 1> ([Shot 1] first frame and last frame): fully_preserved - the orbit starts and ends on this view.\n<Picture 2> ([Shot 1] keyframe at 1.708333 seconds): fully_preserved - the camera passes through this exact view.\n<Picture 3> ([Shot 1] keyframe at 3.416667 seconds): fully_preserved - the camera passes through this exact view.\n\ndetailed_description:\n[Shot 1] The shot begins from <Picture 1>. The camera performs exactly one smooth clockwise 360-degree orbit around the completely stationary <Subject 1>, at constant radius, constant elevation, constant focal length, constant speed, and constant framing, ending at the starting viewpoint. The subject remains perfectly rigid and stationary. No articulation, deformation, secondary motion, wind, zoom, dolly, camera roll, cuts, lighting changes, or scene changes.\n\nAll four milestones below belong to the same uninterrupted [Shot 1], not separate shots. The video runs at 24 fps. Angles describe camera motion clockwise as viewed from above, relative to the starting camera azimuth; the subject itself does not rotate. The camera moves continuously at constant angular speed between these milestones, without pausing, reversing or completing extra turns.\nAt 0.000000 seconds (zero-based frame 0), the camera has advanced 0 degrees clockwise from its starting azimuth; the viewpoint corresponds to <Picture 1>.\nAt 1.708333 seconds (zero-based frame 41), the camera has advanced 120 degrees clockwise from its starting azimuth; the viewpoint corresponds to <Picture 2>.\nAt 3.416667 seconds (zero-based frame 82), the camera has advanced 240 degrees clockwise from its starting azimuth; the viewpoint corresponds to <Picture 3>.\nAt 5.125000 seconds (zero-based frame 123), the camera has advanced 360 degrees clockwise from its starting azimuth; the viewpoint corresponds to <Picture 1>.\n\nThe entire subject is a single frozen three-dimensional scene throughout the shot. Every visible eyelid keeps its reference position: no blinking. Each eye keeps a fixed gaze relative to the head and never tracks the moving camera. Facial expression, mouth, head, hands, feet and body pose remain unchanged. Hair strands, clothing, ribbons, accessories and loose parts are rigidly fixed in the same positions. There is no breathing, sway, settling or secondary motion. Only the camera changes position. Camera radius, elevation, focal length and look-at point stay fixed. Lighting stays fixed in world space; normal viewpoint-dependent shading and reflections remain physically consistent.\n\noverall_soundscape:\nN/A\n\nnon_diegetic_music:\nN/A\n", 1344, 768, 124, "match"], "inputs": [{"name": "clip", "link": 64, "label": "clip", "type": "CLIP", "localized_name": "clip"}, {"shape": 7, "name": "vae", "link": 65, "label": "vae", "type": "VAE", "localized_name": "vae"}, {"shape": 7, "name": "audio_vae", "link": 66, "label": "audio_vae", "type": "VAE", "localized_name": "audio_vae"}, {"shape": 7, "name": "ref_images.ref_image_0", "link": 73, "label": "ref_images.ref_image_0", "type": "IMAGE", "localized_name": "ref_image_0"}, {"shape": 7, "name": "ref_images.ref_image_1", "label": "ref_images.ref_image_1", "type": "IMAGE", "localized_name": "ref_image_1"}, {"shape": 7, "name": "ref_videos.ref_video_0", "label": "ref_videos.ref_video_0", "type": "IMAGE", "localized_name": "ref_video_0"}, {"shape": 7, "name": "ref_video_audios.ref_video_audio_0", "label": "ref_video_audios.ref_video_audio_0", "type": "AUDIO", "localized_name": "ref_video_audio_0"}, {"shape": 7, "name": "ref_audios.ref_audio_0", "label": "ref_audios.ref_audio_0", "type": "AUDIO", "localized_name": "re